# .eos-personal — patterns that should never appear in committed code
# Used by: scripts/check-personal.py, pre-commit hook, CI
# One regex per line. Lines starting with # are comments. Empty lines ignored.
# Add patterns here when you find personal data leaking into code.

# Personal identity — case-insensitive; word-bounded with a short dot-free gap so
# middle-name/initials forms ("KEVIN (BIN) BIAN", "BIAN, Bin") can't slip past
# adjacency-only matching, without flagging the personal domain/handle (binbian.net,
# KevinBean) where the tokens only juxtapose across a dot.
(?i)\bKevin\b[^.\n]{0,12}\bBian\b
(?i)\bBian\b[^.\n]{0,12}\bKevin\b
(?i)\bBian\b[^.\n]{0,12}\bBin\b
bianbin@
bianbin\+

# Current employer — never legitimate in EmptyOS code (Kevin's job is not the product)
\bEnerven\b

# Personal paths
D:\\\\Main Vault
D:/Main Vault
D:\\Main Vault
C:/Users/Kevin
C:\\\\Users\\\\Kevin
C:\\Users\\Kevin

# Personal infrastructure — homepc / tailnet identifiers (must not ship publicly)
100\.91\.167\.57
DESKTOP-3NSTHRB

# Personal coordinates
-34\.928
138\.600

# Personal dates (visa/immigration specific)
# Note: bare dates are OK in comments/examples; these match dates with context
date\(2029,\s*7,\s*1\)
date\(2025,\s*11,\s*25\)
